# quantum-algorithms

## Core Algorithm Components

### Quantum Binary State Analysis (QBSA)
- Analyzes quantum bit sequences to detect state transitions and collapses
- Implements correction ratio calculations to determine system stability
- Processes probe indices against expectations to identify mismatches
- Located in: src/quantum/qbsa.cpp, src/quantum/qbsa_qfh.cpp

### Quantum Fourier Hierarchy (QFH)
- Processes quantum bit sequences to detect state transitions
- Defines three quantum states: NULL_STATE, FLIP, and RUPTURE 
- Calculates rupture and flip ratios for stability determination
- Located in: src/quantum/qfh.cpp

### Pattern Evolution Engine
- Evolves quantum patterns through coherence and stability calculations
- Manages state transitions between memory tiers based on quantum metrics
- Implements mutation mechanics with quantum noise incorporation
- Located in: src/quantum/evolution.cpp

### Quantum Manifold Optimizer
- Optimizes pattern positions within quantum manifold space
- Calculates coherence through Riemannian metric analysis
- Implements gradient descent on manifold surface
- Located in: src/quantum/quantum_manifold_optimizer.cpp

## Memory Integration

### Quantum Coherence Manager
- Tracks coherence across memory tiers using decay rates
- Manages pattern migration based on coherence thresholds:
  - LTM: 0.8f
  - MTM: 0.5f
  - STM: 0.2f
- Located in: src/memory/quantum_coherence_manager.cpp

### Pattern Processing Pipeline
- Handles quantum pattern state evolution
- Maintains coherence history and stability metrics
- Implements pattern collapse detection based on variance analysis
- Located in: src/quantum/pattern_processor.cpp

## Key Business Rules

### State Transitions
- Coherence thresholds determine memory tier placement
- Pattern stability affects promotion/demotion between tiers
- Quantum collapse triggers pattern regeneration
- Rupture detection initiates state correction

### Pattern Evolution
- Mutation rates adapt based on stability metrics
- Coherence decay applies to unstable patterns
- Entanglement strength determines pattern relationships
- Phase correlations influence evolution direction

